      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I believe an income-based distribution approach might be the most equitable way to distribute these units. Relying solely on lottery systems or proximity to transit would favor some people over others based on luck or location rather than need. An income-based approach would ensure that those most in need of affordable housing get the opportunity to benefit from them. However, this could be combined with transit-centric policies to help those who can also benefit from proximity to public transportation.",
